description: High-risk safety and emergency behavior protections
globs:
  - firmware/stage-engine-p4/**
  - firmware/*emergency*/**
  - protocol/*emergency*.h
  - docs/*emergency*.md
  - docs/hardware-pinout.md
---
Safety/emergency constraints:

- Safety changes are high risk and require minimal, explicit modifications.
- Authoritative emergency latch is in P4 show engine path; preserve physical input behavior and clear gates.
- Preserve physical emergency input assumptions (GPIO25 input/latch path as currently implemented).
- Preserve emergency override semantics for outputs, including pixel emergency-white behavior.
- UI/API convenience must never bypass emergency safety path requirements.
- Preserve communications-failure-safe behavior and no-authority-escalation behavior.

For any future safety change, require:
- explicit analysis of current safety path,
- smallest viable implementation,
- compile verification,
- bench-test instructions,
- explicit statement when hardware verification was not performed.
